  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In steady state, the capacitors are fully charged and act as open circuit, so the equivalent circuit in steady state would be as shown:-</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0125_404c3ca29b92.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 114px;\" /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Steady State current is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Potential&nbsp;difference across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Sum of potential difference across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>capacitors is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.&nbsp;As these are in series, so charges on them would be same.&nbsp;Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;be the charge on them, then:-<br />From KVL,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi></math></p>"
  }
